      "writtenOn": "2026-07-16T15:52:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "linux-next is not upstream, but it is a staging ground for the next merge window for upstream.  Changes intended for the next release are staged there, but often linux-next testing will find issues with those patches and they will be modified before being properly merged upstream during the next merge window.\n\nFor patches queued by a maintainer (which is what linux-next pulls together), we use the FROMGIT (ie: \"FROM a maintainers GIT tree\") tag.\n\n\nSimilarly for patches sent to the list, but not yet queued we use FROMLIST.\n\nThis allows the tag to give a sense of confidence that we have in the patch actually going upstream:  FROMLIST(low confidence) -\u003e FROMGIT(higher confidence) -\u003e UPSTREAM (already upstream)",
      "parentUuid": "139658ad_499bf310",
